Rules:
  [P1] Use Pandas for in-memory data processing.
  [P2] Use PySpark for large-scale distributed processing.
  [P3] Use Airflow for workflow orchestration.
  [P4] Implement data quality checks at every pipeline stage.
  [P5] Use Parquet for columnar storage.
  [P6] Implement idempotent data pipelines.
  [P7] Use Dask for parallel computing in Python.
  [P8] Monitor pipeline latency and data freshness.

Pros:
  - Rich data ecosystem
  - Rapid prototyping
  - ML integration

Cons:
  - Memory limitations
  - GIL for CPU-bound work
  - Dependency management

Alternatives:
  - Scala/Spark (big data)
  - Rust (performance)
  - SQL (declarative)

State: +

